---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "Privacy Policy explaining how LionRep Oy processes personal data in connection with HowToWriteYourMemoirs.com.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article>
    <p><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 1, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>

    <p>
      HowToWriteYourMemoirs.com is operated by LionRep Oy.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Data controller:</strong><br />
      LionRep Oy<br />
      Business ID: 3449463-5<br />
      Address: LionRep Oy, PL1 02171 Espoo, Finland<br />
      Finland
    </p>

    <p>
      Privacy enquiries:
      <a href="mailto: kari@lionrep.com">kari@lionrep.com</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. Scope of This Policy</h2>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how LionRep Oy processes personal data when
      you visit HowToWriteYourMemoirs.com, contact us, or follow links from this
      website to third-party services.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Personal Data We Process</h2>

    <h3>Website and security data</h3>

    <p>
      When you visit the website, technical service providers may process
      information such as:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>IP address</li>
      <li>browser and device type</li>
      <li>operating system</li>
      <li>requested pages and files</li>
      <li>date and time of requests</li>
      <li>referring page</li>
      <li>security and error information</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information you send to us</h3>

    <p>
      If you contact us by email, we may process:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>your name</li>
      <li>your email address</li>
      <li>the contents of your message</li>
      <li>any other information you voluntarily provide</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The website currently does not require user accounts, online purchases,
      comments, or newsletter subscriptions.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Purposes and Legal Bases</h2>

    <p>We may process personal data for the following purposes:</p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Legal basis</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Operating and delivering the website</td>
          <td>Legitimate interests</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Maintaining security and preventing abuse</td>
          <td>Legitimate interests</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Responding to messages and enquiries</td>
          <td>Legitimate interests or steps requested by you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Complying with legal obligations</td>
          <td>Legal obligation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Optional analytics or marketing technologies</td>
          <td>Consent, where required</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      Our legitimate interests include operating a secure educational website,
      answering enquiries, protecting the website, and improving its reliability.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Hosting and Technical Service Providers</h2>

    <p>
      The website is hosted using Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may process
      technical request, network, security, and diagnostic information when
      delivering the website.
    </p>

    <p>
      The website source code and content are maintained using GitHub. GitHub
      does not normally receive information submitted by ordinary website
      visitors merely because they visit the published website.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Email Communications</h2>

    <p>
      Messages sent to us may be processed through our email service provider.
    </p>

    <p>
      We use the information in your message to respond, handle your request,
      maintain appropriate records, and protect our legitimate interests.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Analytics and Google Services</h2>

    <p>
      At the date shown above, Google Analytics 4 and Google Tag Manager are not
      active on the website unless a consent mechanism has been implemented and
      you have been given an appropriate choice where required.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before optional analytics technologies are activated, this Privacy Policy
      and the Cookie Policy will be updated to describe the actual configuration,
      purposes, retention settings, recipients, and available consent choices.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google Search Console may be used by the website operator to monitor how
      the website appears in Google Search. It does not require us to place a
      Google Analytics tracking script on pages viewed by visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Amazon and Other External Links</h2>

    <p>
      The website contains links to third-party websites, including Amazon.
      Clicking an external link takes you to a service operated by another
      organisation.
    </p>

    <p>
      Third-party services determine independently how they process personal
      data. Their own terms, privacy policies, cookie practices, and purchasing
      conditions apply.
    </p>

    <p>
      LionRep Oy does not receive your Amazon payment details through this
      website.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Recipients of Personal Data</h2>

    <p>
      Personal data may be disclosed or made available to:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>website hosting and security providers</li>
      <li>email and communication providers</li>
      <li>professional advisers where necessary</li>
      <li>public authorities where required by law</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      We do not sell personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>10. International Data Transfers</h2>

    <p>
      Some service providers may process data outside Finland or the European
      Economic Area.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where required, transfers are protected using an applicable legal transfer
      mechanism, such as an adequacy decision, standard contractual clauses, or
      another safeguard recognised under data protection law.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Retention</h2>

    <p>
      We retain personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for the
      purpose for which it was collected.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        Contact messages may generally be retained for up to 24 months after the
        last relevant communication, unless a longer period is necessary.
      </li>
      <li>
        Security and technical records are retained according to the applicable
        provider's operational and security retention periods.
      </li>
      <li>
        Information required for legal claims or compliance may be retained for
        the applicable statutory period.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>12. Your Data Protection Rights</h2>

    <p>
      Subject to applicable conditions and exceptions, you may have the right to:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>request access to your personal data</li>
      <li>request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
      <li>request deletion of your personal data</li>
      <li>request restriction of processing</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
      <li>receive certain data in a portable format</li>
      <li>withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Withdrawing consent does not affect processing carried out lawfully before
      the withdrawal.
    </p>

    <h2>13. How to Exercise Your Rights</h2>

    <p>
      Send your request to:
      <a href="mailto:[privacy email]">[privacy email]</a>
    </p>

    <p>
      We may need to verify your identity before fulfilling a request. We will
      respond within the period required by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Complaints</h2>

    <p>
      You may lodge a complaint with the Office of the Data Protection Ombudsman
      in Finland or another competent supervisory authority in your country of
      residence or work.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Security</h2>

    <p>
      We use reasonable technical and organisational measures intended to
      protect personal data from unauthorised access, alteration, loss,
      disclosure, or destruction.
    </p>

    <p>
      No internet service can guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Children</h2>

    <p>
      The website is not designed to collect personal information from children.
      If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, please
      contact us.
    </p>

    <h2>17. Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated when the website, technologies, or legal
      requirements change.
    </p>

    <p>
      The current version and its update date will be published on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>18. Contact</h2>

    <p>
      LionRep Oy<br />
      [LionRep Oy address]<br />
      Finland
    </p>

    <p>
      Email:
      <a href="mailto:[privacy email]">[privacy email]</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
